        "src/domain/genesis/systems.clj:114",
        "src/domain/ecs/tick.clj:160",
        "test/architecture_test.clj:63"
      ]
    },
    {
      "subject": "Three-point scope and dependencies",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "rationale": "Three points is a credible proposed estimate for two finite variants, reuse of existing seed preparation/allocation, one materializer integration and narrow registry guards with direct tests. The plan explicitly stops for re-estimation if this needs a general schema, ownership framework, plugin registry or migration of unrelated allocators. It adds neither live-book processing nor cohort settlement. There is no artificial dependency on the pure numerical kernel: later atomic settlement requires both prerequisites and must own final-parent closure before actions. The refinement fixes the old proposed row placement without splitting debit from entity/outcome publication.",
